{"format":1,"manifest":{"name":"fake-data","publisher":"vyloxi","version":"1.0.0","displayName":"Fake Data","description":"Generate realistic people, addresses, companies, products and orders as JSON, CSV, SQL inserts or a JavaScript array, with a seed for repeatable data.","engines":{"ferrum":"^0.1.0"},"categories":["Tools"],"icon":"icon.png","repository":"https://github.com/voukengdongmofrankysteve/ferrum-market","license":"MIT","main":"extension.js","activationEvents":["onCommand:fakeData.people","onCommand:fakeData.addresses","onCommand:fakeData.companies","onCommand:fakeData.products","onCommand:fakeData.orders"],"permissions":[],"contributes":{"commands":[{"command":"fakeData.people","title":"Generate People...","category":"Fake Data"},{"command":"fakeData.addresses","title":"Generate Addresses...","category":"Fake Data"},{"command":"fakeData.companies","title":"Generate Companies...","category":"Fake Data"},{"command":"fakeData.products","title":"Generate Products...","category":"Fake Data"},{"command":"fakeData.orders","title":"Generate Orders...","category":"Fake Data"}],"configuration":{"title":"Fake Data","properties":{"fakeData.seed":{"type":"string","default":"","description":"Any text or number. With a seed the same data comes back every time (good for tests). Empty means different data each time."}}}}},"files":{"icon.png":{"encoding":"base64","content":""},"extension.js":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"// Fake Data: realistic test data (people, addresses, companies, products, orders) as JSON, CSV, SQL inserts or a JavaScript array.\n// A seed makes the same data come back every time, so tests stay stable.\n\nconst FIRST = ['Ada', 'Liam', 'Noah', 'Emma', 'Olivia', 'Lucas', 'Chloe', 'Hugo', 'Lea', 'Mia', 'Ethan', 'Zoe', 'Adam', 'Sara', 'Omar', 'Amina', 'Kofi', 'Fatou', 'Yuki', 'Chen', 'Ivan', 'Elena', 'Mateo', 'Sofia', 'Aiden', 'Nora', 'Jonas', 'Leila', 'Tomas', 'Ines'];\nconst LAST = ['Martin', 'Bernard', 'Dubois', 'Thomas', 'Robert', 'Richard', 'Petit', 'Durand', 'Leroy', 'Moreau', 'Smith', 'Johnson', 'Brown', 'Garcia', 'Kim', 'Nguyen', 'Diallo', 'Mbeki', 'Okafor', 'Tanaka', 'Silva', 'Rossi', 'Muller', 'Novak', 'Haddad', 'Cohen', 'Eze', 'Ndiaye', 'Fofana', 'Mensah'];\nconst CITIES = [['Paris', 'FR'], ['Lyon', 'FR'], ['Montreal', 'CA'], ['Toronto', 'CA'], ['Douala', 'CM'], ['Yaounde', 'CM'], ['Lagos', 'NG'], ['Accra', 'GH'], ['Dakar', 'SN'], ['Berlin', 'DE'], ['Madrid', 'ES'], ['London', 'GB'], ['New York', 'US'], ['Austin', 'US'], ['Tokyo', 'JP']];\nconst STREETS = ['Main Street', 'Oak Avenue', 'Rue de la Paix', 'Maple Road', 'Park Lane', 'Boulevard Central', 'River Street', 'Station Road'];\nconst COMPANIES = ['Acme', 'Globex', 'Initech', 'Umbrella', 'Stark', 'Wayne', 'Hooli', 'Soylent', 'Vandelay', 'Wonka', 'Cyberdyne', 'Tyrell'];\nconst SUFFIX = ['Ltd', 'Inc', 'SARL', 'GmbH', 'Group', 'Labs', 'Studio'];\nconst PRODUCTS = ['Wireless Mouse', 'USB-C Cable', 'Notebook', 'Desk Lamp', 'Water Bottle', 'Backpack', 'Headphones', 'Keyboard', 'Webcam', 'Phone Stand', 'Coffee Mug', 'Laptop Sleeve'];\nconst DOMAINS = ['example.com', 'test.org', 'mail.test', 'demo.dev'];\nconst STATUS = ['pending', 'paid', 'shipped', 'delivered', 'cancelled'];\n\n/** A small seeded random generator (mulberry32): the same seed gives the same numbers. */\nfunction rng(seed) {\n  let a = seed >>> 0;\n  return () => {\n    a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\n    let t = a;\n    t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\n    t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\n    return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n  };\n}\n\nfunction seedFrom(text) {\n  if (/^\\d+$/.test(String(text))) return Number(text);\n  let h = 2166136261;\n  for (const c of String(text)) h = Math.imul(h ^ c.charCodeAt(0), 16777619);\n  return h >>> 0;\n}\n\nconst slug = (s) => s.toLowerCase().normalize('NFD').replace(/[̀-ͯ]/g, '').replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '.').replace(/^\\.|\\.$/g, '');\n\nfunction make(kind, n, seed) {\n  const r = rng(seed);\n  const pick = (a) => a[Math.floor(r() * a.length)];\n  const int = (lo, hi) => lo + Math.floor(r() * (hi - lo + 1));\n  const date = (y0, y1) => new Date(Date.UTC(int(y0, y1), int(0, 11), int(1, 28), int(0, 23), int(0, 59))).toISOString();\n  const uuid = () => {\n    const h = () => Math.floor(r() * 0xffff).toString(16).padStart(4, '0');\n    return h() + h() + '-' + h() + '-4' + h().slice(1) + '-a' + h().slice(1) + '-' + h() + h() + h();\n  };\n  const rows = [];\n  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {\n    if (kind === 'people') {\n      const f = pick(FIRST);\n      const l = pick(LAST);\n      const [city, country] = pick(CITIES);\n      rows.push({ id: i, name: f + ' ' + l, email: slug(f + ' ' + l) + int(1, 99) + '@' + pick(DOMAINS), age: int(18, 75), city, country, createdAt: date(2022, 2025) });\n    } else if (kind === 'addresses') {\n      const [city, country] = pick(CITIES);\n      rows.push({ id: i, street: int(1, 999) + ' ' + pick(STREETS), city, postalCode: String(int(10000, 99999)), country });\n    } else if (kind === 'companies') {\n      const name = pick(COMPANIES) + ' ' + pick(SUFFIX);\n      rows.push({ id: i, name, domain: slug(name.split(' ')[0]) + '.com', employees: int(3, 5000), city: pick(CITIES)[0], founded: int(1985, 2023) });\n    } else if (kind === 'products') {\n      const name = pick(PRODUCTS);\n      rows.push({ id: i, sku: 'SKU-' + String(int(1000, 9999)), name, price: Math.round(r() * 9000 + 500) / 100, stock: int(0, 400), inStock: r() > 0.15 });\n    } else if (kind === 'orders') {\n      rows.push({ id: uuid(), customerId: int(1, 50), product: pick(PRODUCTS), quantity: int(1, 6), total: Math.round(r() * 30000 + 800) / 100, status: pick(STATUS), placedAt: date(2024, 2025) });\n    } else throw new Error('Unknown kind ' + kind);\n  }\n  return rows;\n}\n\nconst csvCell = (v) => (/[\",\\n]/.test(String(v)) ? '\"' + String(v).replace(/\"/g, '\"\"') + '\"' : String(v));\n\nfunction format(rows, as, table) {\n  if (as === 'json') return JSON.stringify(rows, null, 2);\n  if (as === 'js') return 'const ' + table + ' = ' + JSON.stringify(rows, null, 2).replace(/\"([A-Za-z_]\\w*)\":/g, '$1:').replace(/\"/g, \"'\") + ';';\n  const keys = Object.keys(rows[0] || {});\n  if (as === 'csv') return [keys.join(','), ...rows.map((r) => keys.map((k) => csvCell(r[k])).join(','))].join('\\n');\n  if (as === 'sql') {\n    const lit = (v) => (typeof v === 'number' ? String(v) : typeof v === 'boolean' ? (v ? 'TRUE' : 'FALSE') : \"'\" + String(v).replace(/'/g, \"''\") + \"'\");\n    return rows.map((r) => 'INSERT INTO ' + table + ' (' + keys.join(', ') + ') VALUES (' + keys.map((k) => lit(r[k])).join(', ') + ');').join('\\n');\n  }\n  throw new Error('Unknown format ' + as);\n}\n\nexports._test = { make, format, rng, seedFrom, slug };\n\nexports.activate = function (context) {\n  async function generate(kind) {\n    const nText = await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'How many ' + kind + '?', value: '10' });\n    if (nText === undefined) return;\n    const n = Math.max(1, Math.min(2000, Math.floor(Number(nText)) || 10));\n    const as = await ferrum.window.showQuickPick([{ label: 'JSON', v: 'json' }, { label: 'CSV', v: 'csv' }, { label: 'SQL INSERT statements', v: 'sql' }, { label: 'JavaScript array', v: 'js' }], { placeholder: 'Output format' });\n    if (!as) return;\n    const seedSetting = String(ferrum.settings.get('fakeData.seed') || '').trim();\n    const seed = seedSetting ? seedFrom(seedSetting) : Math.floor(Math.random() * 4294967295);\n    await ferrum.editor.insert(format(make(kind, n, seed), as.v, kind));\n  }\n  context.subscriptions.push(\n    ...['people', 'addresses', 'companies', 'products', 'orders'].map((k) => ferrum.commands.register('fakeData.' + k, () => generate(k))),\n  );\n};\n\nexports.deactivate = function () {};\n"},"README.md":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"# Fake Data\n\nRun a command, say how many (up to 2000) and pick the output: **JSON**, **CSV**, **SQL INSERT statements** or a **JavaScript array**. The data is inserted at the cursor.\n\n| Kind | Fields |\n| --- | --- |\n| People | id, name, email, age, city, country, createdAt |\n| Addresses | id, street, city, postalCode, country |\n| Companies | id, name, domain, employees, city, founded |\n| Products | id, sku, name, price, stock, inStock |\n| Orders | id (uuid), customerId, product, quantity, total, status, placedAt |\n\nSet **Fake Data: Seed** in settings (for example `demo`) and you get the same rows every time, so your tests do not change from run to run. Names are only plausible combinations; the data is not real. No permissions needed.\n"}}}